WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.660
Welcome to our training on Amazon anti-counterfeiting policy compliance.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.360
The tips we'll share in this video don't take the place of legal advice.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.980
So, remember to consult a lawyer.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:19.700
If you have any specific anti-counterfeiting or intellectual property questions, when you list products

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.400
in the Amazon store, you'll need to comply with all applicable laws and Amazon policies.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.180
One of these policies is the Amazon anti-counterfeiting policy.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.420
Which helps ensure that all products in the Amazon store are authentic.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.900
When you sell in the Amazon store, you agree that all of your products are authentic.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:48.879
Some examples of inauthentic or counterfeit products include bootlegs, fakes, pirated copies of

00:00:48.879 --> 00:00:50.720
products or content.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:59.236
Products that have been illegally replicated, reproduced, or manufactured, and products that infringe

00:00:59.236 --> 00:01:01.900
on another party's intellectual property rights.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:09.330
To help avoid selling counterfeit and inauthentic products, we recommend sourcing your products

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.750
from a reliable supplier and verifying that they're authentic.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:19.350
Before you list them, in certain cases, an Amazon selling partner will list an authentic product,

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:22.680
but customers or other sellers might think it's inauthentic.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:30.573
To help avoid this misunderstanding, we recommend listing and shipping products in the, manufacturer's

00:01:30.573 --> 00:01:37.120
original packaging, and refraining from altering or removing the brand's packaging, which contains

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.800
important product information.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:41.860
Let's review an example of a product listing.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.600
That doesn't comply with our anti-counterfeiting policy.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:45.212
A seller lists a handbag in the Amazon store.

00:01:45.212 --> 00:01:53.780
On its product detail page, the seller notes that the handbag is from brand ABC.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:02:00.000
A customer sees the product listing, notices the brand name product's low price, and makes a purchase.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.904
When the handbag arrives, the customer discovers that the handbag isn't one of the brand's authentic

00:02:05.904 --> 00:02:07.380
products and contacts Amazon.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:13.820
In this example, the seller has violated the Amazon anti-counterfeiting policy.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:19.380
Sellers who don't comply with this or other selling policies may experience the following.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:22.940
The listings that are in violation may be suspended.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:29.900
Their funds may be withheld in accordance with applicable laws or Amazon's funds withholding policy.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:36.580
Their FBA product inventory may be removed or disposed of in accordance with applicable laws or

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.580
Amazon's business solutions agreement.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.380
And their selling account may be either suspended or deactivated.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:49.380
When you and other sellers comply with the anti-counterfeiting policy, you help ensure customers

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:52.580
can trust the products they buy in the Amazon store.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:59.750
To review the Amazon anti-counterfeiting policy, search for anti-counterfeiting policy in Seller

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:00.180
Central.

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:08.260
This concludes our training on how to comply with the Amazon anti-counterfeiting policy.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:12.980
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
